+### 3.8 `/terrain_advisory` (Receive-only terrain status)
+
+- **Type:** `std_msgs/msg/Float64MultiArray`; Best Effort.
+- **`data` (exactly 8 finite values):**
+
+| Index | Field | Accepted values |
+|:---:|---|---|
+| `0` | Classification code | Integer: `0` NONE, `1` JUMP_CANDIDATE, `2` STOP_CANDIDATE, `3` UNCERTAIN |
+| `1` | `distance_m` | `>= 0` |
+| `2` | `height_m` | `>= 0` |
+| `3` | `width_m` | `>= 0` |
+| `4` | `confidence` | `[0, 1]` |
+| `5` | `plane_valid` | `0` or `1` |
+| `6` | `sequence` | Finite sequence value; acknowledged as UInt32 |
+| `7` | `age_s` | Finite source age in seconds |
+
+Messages with a wrong length, non-finite values, invalid code/plane flag, negative geometry, or out-of-range confidence are rejected and counted. Rejected messages do not refresh freshness. The MCU uses its own receive tick: after 300 ms without a valid message, the reported state becomes UNCERTAIN. At boot, before the first valid message, it is stale/UNCERTAIN. This advisory is display and telemetry only; it does not change motor commands, modes, watchdogs, or RC behavior.
+
+```bash
+ros2 topic pub -r 10 /terrain_advisory std_msgs/msg/Float64MultiArray \
+  "{data: [2.0, 0.99, 0.13, 0.40, 0.95, 1.0, 42.0, 0.02]}"
+```
+
+### 3.9 `/terrain_advisory_ack` (Last accepted sequence)
+
+- **Type:** `std_msgs/msg/UInt32`; Reliable, published at 10 Hz.
+- **Data:** index 6 from the last accepted `/terrain_advisory` message converted to UInt32 (fractional values truncate; values below zero map to zero and values above UInt32 range map to `4294967295`). Before any valid message, this is zero. The value remains at the last accepted sequence if messages stop or a later message is rejected.
+
+```bash
+ros2 topic echo /terrain_advisory_ack
+```
+
